  "query_preview": "Outlook...\n\nFor the remainder of the work week, beginning Wednesday,\nconditions will trend drier and slightly cooler. Sprawling \nCanadian high-pressure will spread southeast across the Midwest,\nkeeping high temperatures in the mid to upper 70s Wednesday \nthrough Friday, with no measurable precipitation through \nThursday. By Thursday night, a signal for warm advection-driven \nconvection develops to our west, resulting in a 20-30% chance of\nstorms on Friday west of Fulton Co to Shelby Co. A warming \ntrend will commence next weekend as the surface ridge axis \nshifts to our east, allowing for a return of warmer southerly \nflow.",
